  << /ActualText (We investigate the reasoning process of a human reviewer and summarize it into four reasoning steps\072\0501\051 Interpreting code changes\054 2\051 Planning what to check\054 3\051 Analyzing individual check items and 4\051 Summary the results into a review\056\nWe then design our multi\055LLM framework\054 where each stage maps to a specific human reasoning step\056 This design allows us to\072\nSeparate the information needed for different stages\054 avoiding putting all context into a single iteration\056\nKeep the process transparent\054 ensuring the model follows the same reasoning process as a human\056\nAllow different stages to use specialized models\056\nAt each stage\054 we use retrieval\055augmented generation \050RAG\051 to provide relevant project context and knowledge to the model\054 enabling more informed and context\055aware code review\056 For any project to be used\054 we first index its project context using an Extract\054 Transform\054 Load \050ETL\051 pipeline\054 which is responsible for extracting paragraphs from documents\054 transforming them into semantically meaningful chunks\054 and loading these chunks into a vector database\056 WWe currently use Spring AI as our test project\054 using its full source code repository and documentation as the project context\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 931 0 R
     /Pg 918 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

