936 0 obj
  << /ActualText (We evaluate on 10 real pull requests from the Spring AI GitHub repository\054 selected by two criteria\072 PR description \07650 words\054 and \07610 human comments\056 We compare four systems\072 CodeRabbit\054 GitHub Copilot\054 SingleLLM \050our system with only the summary stage\051\054 and our full system\056\nComment\055alignment\072 measures how closely the generated review matches human comments\056 Human comments are rephrased by an LLM into atomic reference sentences\073 generated reviews are split into candidate sentences\073 SentenceBERT matches candidate\023reference pairs to compute Precision \057 Recall \057 F1\056\nInterpretation\055alignment\072 measures how well the generated code\055change interpretation matches the original PR description\054 computed the same way but using the PR description as the reference\056)
     /K [ 9 ]
     /P 937 0 R
     /Pg 918 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

937 0 obj
  << /K [ 936 0 R ]
     /P 952 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 918 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

938 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Comment\055alignment\072 LLMCR \050our system\051 achieved the highest F1 score among all groups\054 showing its reviews align most closely with human comments\056\nInterpretation\055alignment\072 LLMCR scored lower than Copilot but slightly higher than CodeRabbit \024 indicating it\047s not yet as strong at understanding code changes\056)
     /K [ 10 ]
     /P 939 0 R
     /Pg 918 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
